Medicine Details
Stores medicine information.
Includes medicine name, medicine ID, price, expiry date, and category.
Helps to easily search and manage medicines.
Supplier Details
Stores supplier information.
Includes supplier name, supplier ID, phone number, and address.
Helps to manage medicine suppliers.
Stock
Maintains the available medicine stock.
Updates stock when new medicines are added.
Helps to know the current quantity of medicines.
Sale
Records medicines sold to customers.
Stores sale details such as medicine, quantity, price, and total amount.
Helps to maintain sales records.
Quantity
Keeps track of the quantity of each medicine.
Quantity increases when new stock is added.
Quantity decreases when medicines are sold.
Helps to avoid stock shortages.
Objective
The main objective of the Medicine Management System is to manage medicine details, supplier details, stock, sales, and quantity in an easy and organized way.
Conclusion
The Medicine Management System helps to manage medicines and their stock efficiently. It reduces manual work and keeps medicine and sales information properly organized.
